# dotfiles

This is a collection of dotfiles for my development environment.

## Setup

```bash
export MY_DOTFILES_DIR="$HOME/.my_dotfiles"
git clone https://github.com/zyksir/dotfiles.git $MY_DOTFILES_DIR && bash $MY_DOTFILES_DIR/setup.sh && zsh
```

`setup.sh`:

1. Installs the Claude Code CLI with Anthropic's native installer when `claude`
   is not already available.
2. Adds `~/.local/bin` to `PATH` for the setup process and future Zsh sessions.
3. Verifies the installation with `claude --version`.
4. Copies every skill under `skills/` into both `~/.claude/skills/` and
   `~/.cursor/skills/`.

The first interactive `claude` session may still require authentication.

## Agent skills

Personal skills live under `skills/<skill-name>/SKILL.md`.

Current skills:

- `technical-blog-writing` — write and edit evidence-backed engineering posts
- `code-object-design` — design and review maintainable Python, C++, and CUDA code

### Loading and invocation

Claude Code and Cursor discover these installed skills automatically. They see
each skill's name and description, then load its full instructions only when the
task is relevant. No separate enable command is required.

To force a specific skill, invoke it by name:

```text
/technical-blog-writing Write a post from these benchmark notes.
/code-object-design Review this CUDA API without over-engineering it.
```

Start a new Claude Code or Cursor session after running setup so the installed
skills are discovered.

Filesystem installation applies to Claude Code or Cursor running on that
machine, including a cloud VM where `setup.sh` was executed. Claude.ai-managed
cloud sessions use skills enabled on the Claude account instead; they do not
read `~/.claude/skills/` from another machine.
